WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:01.520
STEPHANIE WONG:
What's up, everyone.

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.020
Thanks for checking out "This
Week In Cloud," where we serve

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:05.710
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:07.510
Our Google Cloud
Platform region in Zurich

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:09.680
is now live and
ready for business.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.080
Let's do this with numbers.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:14.260
It's our sixth European
region, and our 19th worldwide.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:17.800
And the Zurich GCP region comes
with three availability zones.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.050
But the coolest number,
hosting applications here

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:22.090
can improve latency
for Swiss end users

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:23.928
by up to 10 milliseconds.

00:00:23.928 --> 00:00:25.720
You'll have access to
our flagship products

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.240
such as Google Compute
Engine, Google Kubernetes

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.250
Engine, BitQuery, and so on.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.403
But best of all, thanks
to Cloud Interconnect,

00:00:32.403 --> 00:00:35.070
you can even access the services
that aren't available in Zurich

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.540
yet by connecting to other
regions over the Google

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:38.310
network.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:41.538
Try it out and reach
end users worldwide.

00:00:41.538 --> 00:00:44.080
You might know that Google wrote
the book on site reliability

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:44.920
engineering.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.110
And now we're adding
some new chapters.

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:49.510
We've just added a new
Coursera course on SRE

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:52.360
to help engineers design and
manage complex systems that

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:54.280
meet their reliability targets.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.020
Basically it distills
everything we've

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:58.360
learned through trial and
error about SRE since we

00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.860
coined the term itself.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:03.070
These best practices are tried
and true, so check them out.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:05.770
Not sure where to get started
on these best practices?

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:07.360
Our Google Cloud
partners have access

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.310
to lots of great
resources, including

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:11.920
helping you discover new
solutions for your customers

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.010
and new channels for your
business with Google Cloud.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.148
Our SLO guide is a free
resource for our partners

00:01:17.148 --> 00:01:18.940
to help companies
discover what they should

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:21.610
measure based on common
architectures and critical user

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:22.528
journeys.

00:01:22.528 --> 00:01:24.820
So if you want to see what
being a Google Cloud partner

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.510
can do for you, take a look at
the path to becoming a partner.

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:31.150
Speaking of better SRE,
have you tried out Istio

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:33.880
and see how it can support
your SRE practices?

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:36.130
Check out this awesome
blog from our Istio series

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:37.750
to discover how
to easily surface

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:41.173
application metrics with Istio
and Stackdriver monitoring.

00:01:41.173 --> 00:01:43.090
You'll even learn how
to track the progression

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:46.120
of a single request as it's
handled by our other services

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.497
in your deployment
with Stackdriver Trace,

00:01:48.497 --> 00:01:50.080
while Stackdriver
Logging can give you

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.032
a more complete picture of what
your app is doing at all times.

00:01:53.032 --> 00:01:55.240
Read the blog post, and try
out the hands-on tutorial

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:56.187
for yourself.

00:01:56.187 --> 00:01:58.270
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:00.490
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:01.780
Have thoughts or ideas?

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.380
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:05.850
We'll see you in the cloud.

